# COM_POISSON Python Package

A Python 3.9+ implementation of adaptive filtering for Conway-Maxwell-Poisson (CMP)
distributions, primarily for neuronal spike data analysis.

This package is a complete conversion of the original MATLAB codebase from
[weigcdsb/COM_POISSON](https://github.com/weigcdsb/COM_POISSON).

## Package Structure

```
com_poisson/
├── distribution/     CMP distribution (PDF, RNG, moments, log-sum)
├── smoother/         Adaptive filtering & RTS smoothing
├── optimization/     Newton-Raphson optimiser and helpers
├── basis/            B-spline basis functions
└── utils/            Utility functions
```

## Installation

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
# or, if you have a local clone:
pip install -e .
```

**Requirements:** Python ≥ 3.9, NumPy ≥ 1.22, SciPy ≥ 1.8

## Quick Start

```python
import numpy as np
from com_poisson.distribution import CMPmoment, com_pdf, com_rnd
from com_poisson.smoother import ppasmoo_compoisson_fisher_na
from com_poisson.basis import getCubicBSplineBasis

# --- CMP distribution ---
lam, nu = 5.0, 1.5
mean_Y, var_Y, *_ = CMPmoment(lam, nu)
print(f"mean={mean_Y:.3f}, var={var_Y:.3f}")

probs = com_pdf(np.arange(15), lam, nu)
samples = com_rnd(lam, nu, N=100)

# --- B-spline basis ---
x = np.linspace(0, 1, 200)
B = getCubicBSplineBasis(x, nknots=8)   # (200, 9)

# --- CMP adaptive smoother ---
T = 50
X_lam = np.tile(B[:T, :], (1, 1))
G_nu  = np.ones((T, 1))
theta0 = np.zeros(X_lam.shape[1] + G_nu.shape[1])
W0 = np.eye(len(theta0))
F  = np.eye(len(theta0))
Q  = 1e-4 * np.eye(len(theta0))
spk = np.random.poisson(3.0, size=(1, T)).astype(float)

theta, W, *_ = ppasmoo_compoisson_fisher_na(theta0, spk, X_lam, G_nu, W0, F, Q)
```

## Demo

```bash
python demo/demo_glm.py
```

The demo simulates a 100-orientation × 100-trial CMP dataset with a
drifting tuning curve and fits an adaptive CMP GLM.

## Module Reference

### `com_poisson.distribution`
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `CMPmoment(lam, nu)` | Compute E[Y], Var[Y], E[log Y!], Var[log Y!], Cov(Y, log Y!), log Z |
| `com_pdf(n, lam, nu)` | CMP probability mass function |
| `com_rnd(lam, nu, N)` | Random sampling from CMP |
| `logsum_calc(lam, nu, n)` | Numerically stable log-sum terms |
| `varParam(X_lam, G_nu, theta, W)` | Delta-method variance of fitted rate |

### `com_poisson.smoother`
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `ppasmoo_compoisson_fisher_na(...)` | CMP forward-backward smoother (Fisher scoring) |
| `ppafilt_compoisson_fisher_na(...)` | CMP forward filter |
| `ppasmoo_cmp_fixNu_na(...)` | CMP smoother with fixed ν |
| `ppasmoo_poissexp_nan(...)` | Poisson forward-backward smoother |
| `ppafilt_poissexp_nan(...)` | Poisson forward filter |

### `com_poisson.optimization`
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `newtonGH(fdf, x0, ...)` | Newton-Raphson optimiser |
| `gradHessTheta_na(...)` | CMP gradient/Hessian (free ν) |
| `gradHessTheta_CMP_fixNu_na(...)` | CMP gradient/Hessian (fixed ν) |
| `gradHessTheta_Poisson_nan(...)` | Poisson gradient/Hessian |
| `blktridiag(Amd, Asub, Asup)` | Sparse block tridiagonal matrix |
| `llhdCMP_consNu_na(nu, X, theta, spk)` | CMP log-likelihood (constant ν) |
| `helper_na(Q, ...)` | CMP process-noise optimisation objective |
| `helper_poisson_nan(Q, ...)` | Poisson process-noise optimisation objective |

### `com_poisson.basis`
| Function / Class | Description |
|------------------|-------------|
| `fastBSpline(knots, weights)` | B-spline class with `evalAt`, `getBasis`, `dx`, `lsqspline`, `pspline` |
| `getCubicBSplineBasis(x, nknots, isCirc)` | Cubic B-spline design matrix |
| `getSpkMat(Tlist, dt, T, isLogical)` | Spike matrix from spike-time arrays |
| `fitXcorrSpline(x, y, nknots)` | Smooth cross-correlogram with a P-spline |

